## Execution and assessment contract

Every indexed lesson has complete reasoning, a worked example, supported completion, two immediate full checks, two delayed full variants, exact keys, misconception corrections and a condition-aware rubric. Normally two distinct unused I checks establish acquisition; an unused D check is an explicitly permitted full substitute and then unavailable as delayed evidence. All six two-item combinations of I1,I2,D1,D2 have complete component coverage because each item elicits and keys the entire objective. Narrow corrections, diagnostics and exposed examples are never substitutes. Repeated exposed items do not count. Exhausted bank or an uncovered alternative generates plan_issue. Teach retrieves this index and one lesson; recall alone assigns due dates.

